Which type of relationship does this graph show?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-4,xmax=4,ymin=-7,ymax=3,xtick={-4,-3,...,4},ytick={-6,-4,...,2},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-2.7:2.7,samples=100] {-x*x+2};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which type of relationship does this graph show?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-3,xmax=3,ymin=-1,ymax=10,xtick={-3,-2,...,3},ytick={0,2,...,10},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-2.1:2.9,samples=100] {exp(-x*ln(3))};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which type of relationship does this graph show?
